 \section*{Null-space experiment}
 \begin{itemize}
-\item To study this case, we added a commanded torque disturbance equivalent to a virtual force of 20 newtons on link three. Through the Jacobian mapping, this disturbance acted mainly on joint one, while the captured Cartesian pose remained the reference.
-\item We compare four conditions with three trials each: no null-space torque, damping alone, conditioning alone, and both torques together. The enabled settings are 2 newton metres for conditioning and 2 newton metre seconds per radian for damping.
